WEB SERVICES :
-->  Web Service is a way for two different applications to communicate with each other over a network (usually the Internet) 
and exchange data.
--> It allows one application to request information or perform an action on another application.
Types of Web Services :
1. SOAP Web Services : SOAP = Simple Object Access Protocol
Features :
--> Highly secure
--> Strict rules
--> Uses XML only

2. REST Web Services : REST = Representational State Transfer
Features :
--> Fast
--> Lightweight
--> Easy to develop
Today most applications use REST APIs.

SOAP vs REST :
| Feature     | SOAP      | REST      |
| ----------- | --------- | --------- |
| Data Format | XML       | JSON/XML  |
| Speed       | Slower    | Faster    |
| Complexity  | High      | Low       |
| Learning    | Difficult | Easy      |
| Popularity  | Less      | Very High |

REST Concepts :
1. Resource : A Resource is any data or object that the API exposes.
2. Representation : Resources are stored internally in one format but sent to clients in another format.
This format is called a Representation.
--> Data Representation format is JSON or XML
3. Statelessness : REST APIs are stateless., The server does not remember previous requests.
Every request should contain all required information.
